                        "form": "пе́нсах"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e96926ba-e4a3-3588-b229-e9f2a2e4e359",
                        "entry_id": "eeb69837-649c-30c2-ae6b-b7fb7b2311eb",
                        "glosses": [
                            "нумизм. то же, что британский пенни; мелкая английская, позже британская монета (до февраля 1971 года пенни был равен 1⁄12 шиллинга или 1⁄240 фунта стерлингов, с 1971 года по настоящее время = 1⁄100 фунта стерлингов)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d117ed75-6d3a-4bff-9ceb-7771262469f6",
                                "sense_id": "e96926ba-e4a3-3588-b229-e9f2a2e4e359",
                                "text": "Фунт стерлингов равняется 20 шиллингам, шиллинг — 12 пенсам, пенс — 4 фартингам."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b57a7914-ec47-454a-9481-1ba15a2afff8",
                                "sense_id": "e96926ba-e4a3-3588-b229-e9f2a2e4e359",
                                "text": "Неважно, что с восьми фунтов вы получаете сдачу всего один пенс, цена выглядит всё же семь фунтов, а не восемь."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "51fd8335-de27-491a-856c-41df3c741bd9",
                                "sense_id": "e96926ba-e4a3-3588-b229-e9f2a2e4e359",
                                "text": "«Пять фунтов ячменя, пять фунтов кукурузы, на 3 пенса селёдок (пенс — английская монета, составлявшая тогда одну двестисороковую часть фунта стерлингов; с февраля 1971 года 1 фунт стерлингов = 100 пенсам. — Прим. автора), на 1 пенс соли, на 1 пенс уксуса, на 2 пенса перцу и зелени, итого на сумму 20 пенсов получается суп на 64 человека»."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7b9faade-2c2f-4c51-941a-b803cad5b22c",
                        "source_entry_id": "eeb69837-649c-30c2-ae6b-b7fb7b2311eb",
                        "source_sense_id": "e96926ba-e4a3-3588-b229-e9f2a2e4e359",
                        "target_lang_word": "penny",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "penny",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8badcdbb-308a-30e1-a641-d1896b99693b",
                                        "entry_id": "d713f754-4e14-39b3-86ad-43037df71fe2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In the United Kingdom and Ireland and many other countries, a unit of currency worth ¹⁄₂₄₀ of a pound sterling or Irish pound before decimalisation, or a copper coin worth this amount. Abbreviation: d."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "acfa5250-ef70-42f4-82bc-e41d5914459b",
                                                "sense_id": "8badcdbb-308a-30e1-a641-d1896b99693b",
                                                "text": "Thanks to that penny he had just spent so recklessly [on a newspaper] he would pass a happy hour, taken, for once, out of his anxious, despondent, miserable self. It irritated him shrewdly to know that these moments of respite from carking care would not be shared with his poor wife, with careworn, troubled Ellen."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d15397c2-72e7-430c-8e1c-a00e7dc034ed",
                                                "sense_id": "8badcdbb-308a-30e1-a641-d1896b99693b",
                                                "text": "We had not proceeded very far across the south cantilever when we saw a penny lying beside the track, and another a short distance further on. We were to find several more pennies, and some half-pennies, before we reached the north shore. Inspector Bell explained that many passengers try to throw a coin into the Forth, for \"good luck,\" while trains are crossing the bridge."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cfa745f4-23f0-4039-9699-7c672c702802",
                                                "sense_id": "8badcdbb-308a-30e1-a641-d1896b99693b",
                                                "text": "However he lost out, as other business interests whom he had alienated by his efforts to squeeze every penny of profit from the canal, supported the construction of the railway."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e1a70959-aba3-32fe-9215-d91e6d192796",
                                        "entry_id": "d713f754-4e14-39b3-86ad-43037df71fe2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In the United Kingdom, a unit of currency worth ¹⁄₁₀₀ of a pound sterling, or a copper coin worth this amount. Abbreviation: p."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "be76ca97-1aa2-3a43-98c6-ed045657f13e",
                                        "entry_id": "d713f754-4e14-39b3-86ad-43037df71fe2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In Ireland, a coin worth ¹⁄₁₀₀ of an Irish pound before the introduction of the euro. Abbreviation: p."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "19ecf7c4-f657-35b8-8872-e5276f7e3ad8",
                                        "entry_id": "d713f754-4e14-39b3-86ad-43037df71fe2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In the US and (formerly) Canada, a one-cent coin, worth ¹⁄₁₀₀ of a dollar. Abbreviation: ¢."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a4f7d9d2-801c-4da0-852f-14243e696c38",
                                                "sense_id": "19ecf7c4-f657-35b8-8872-e5276f7e3ad8",
                                                "text": "Holy shit! A hundred and eleven pennies! At that point, that dog had more Lincoln in him than Mary Todd."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "89d84a66-af53-3d7d-b8f7-8e87c2e981eb",
                                        "entry_id": "d713f754-4e14-39b3-86ad-43037df71fe2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In various countries, a small-denomination copper or brass coin."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a590a0d8-06f4-3bc4-a22c-ac12bda53e21",
                                        "entry_id": "d713f754-4e14-39b3-86ad-43037df71fe2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A unit of nail size, said to be either the cost per 100 nails, or the number of nails per penny. Abbreviation: d."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2b331cb0-94fc-33e4-a3cf-471a8f6ff481",
                                        "entry_id": "d713f754-4e14-39b3-86ad-43037df71fe2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Money in general."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7d00baac-c671-4ba6-9971-502b1b356d17",
                                                "sense_id": "2b331cb0-94fc-33e4-a3cf-471a8f6ff481",
                                                "text": "to turn an honest penny"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65ba50d6-9e45-4abb-b53f-623165672c67",
                                                "sense_id": "2b331cb0-94fc-33e4-a3cf-471a8f6ff481",
                                                "text": "What penny hath Rome borne, / What men provided, what munition sent?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "penny",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "60491edd-07d9-3211-a466-3b7635b81a68",
                                        "entry_id": "d57d30a5-0304-331b-9082-41e6f6eb263a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To jam a door shut by inserting pennies between the doorframe and the door."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab0b0e24-4b0e-4307-ad2a-1012d18c3652",
                                                "sense_id": "60491edd-07d9-3211-a466-3b7635b81a68",
                                                "text": "Zach and Ben had only been at college for a week when their door was pennied by the girls down the hall."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2e662770-f1cd-359c-a818-f17b6a0fa3ca",
                                        "entry_id": "d57d30a5-0304-331b-9082-41e6f6eb263a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To circumvent the tripping of an electrical circuit breaker by the dangerous practice of inserting a coin in place of a fuse in a fuse socket."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6c1ec2a6-c58e-3983-8eaa-6422333420f7",
                                        "entry_id": "d57d30a5-0304-331b-9082-41e6f6eb263a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "During a meal or as part of a drinking game, to drop a penny in a person's drink with the expectation that they finish it (or some such variation thereof); commonly associated with crewdates at Oxford and swaps at Cambridge."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9b68b50-597c-47bb-b971-b5c587fec4b6",
                                                "sense_id": "6c1ec2a6-c58e-3983-8eaa-6422333420f7",
                                                "text": "You got pennied! Down it, fresher."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
